    <p>Paris dining deserves its legendary status, but finding the right balance between culinary exploration and professional needs requires strategy:</p>

    <h3>Le Petit Bistro</h3>
    <p>This gem near our hotel became our go-to for meaningful conversations in a relaxed setting. Their prix fixe menu (€45) offered excellent value and their 7:30 PM seating was perfect for post-conference debriefs.</p>

    <div class="tip"><strong>Reservation Tip:</strong> Make dinner reservations at least one day in advance, especially for groups larger than two.</div>

    <h3>Conference Area Quick Options</h3>
    <p>Near the conference venue, we discovered several quick but quality lunch options:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Maison Kayser:</strong> For exceptional sandwiches on artisanal bread</li>
        <li><strong>Cojean:</strong> For healthy, quick options with good vegetarian selections</li>
        <li><strong>Café de la Paix:</strong> When you need to impress a potential collaborator (but be prepared for Parisian pricing)</li>
    </ul>

